  "question": {
    "text": "The number of arrangements of the letters of the word &quot;INDEPENDENCE&quot;&nbsp;in which all the vowels always occur together is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16800</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>33600</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18000</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14800</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>There are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;vowels in the given word which are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>E</mi><mo>'</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#8201;</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>I</mi></math>.</p><p>Since they have to always occur together we take&nbsp;them as a single object&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;for the time being.</p><p>This single object together with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;remaining object will account for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;objects.</p><p>There&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;objects in which there are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#8201;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>D</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>s</mi></math>&nbsp;can be arrangement in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;ways.</p><p>Corresponding to each of their arrangements the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;vowels&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;which can be arranged in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, required number of arrangements.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>16800</mn></math></p><p>Hence this is the correct option.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}